# The consumer cross-checks its own totals against data/history.csv, so that
# file has to be byte-stable for reasons beyond tidiness: anything that
# rewrites it turns the cross-check into a comparison of one side's output
# with itself. Python's csv module defaults to CRLF; the collector now pins
# LF, and git is told to keep it that way whatever wrote the file last.
data/history.csv text eol=lf
*.json text eol=lf
*.md text eol=lf
*.py text eol=lf
*.yml text eol=lf
# data/servers.csv is deliberately not listed yet. Declaring it while HEAD
# still holds CRLF makes every checkout look modified until the file is
# renormalised, and renormalising a 36,000-line file is a full-file diff that
# trips the local pre-push credential scanner on repository names. The
# collector writes LF now; once a CI run has committed it that way, widen
# this line to *.csv.
